Pre-existing, not caused by #72 -- reproduced against a pristine `git archive
HEAD` tree. t/images.t line 61, the live branch of the 'inspect image'
subtest:

  my $name = $images->[0]->RepoTags ? $images->[0]->RepoTags->[0]
                                    : $images->[0]->Id;

An untagged image answers `RepoTags => []`. An empty ArrayRef is TRUE, so the
ternary takes the tag branch and `->[0]` is undef; inspect(undef) then croaks
'Image name required' and the subtest dies with no plan.

Measured 2026-08-28 against the rootless Podman socket
(unix:///run/user/1000/podman/podman.sock, API 1.41), whose store holds two
<none>:<none> images sorted ahead of the tagged ones:

  sha256:28cf8998...  RepoTags=[]
  sha256:a9d745d1...  RepoTags=[]
  sha256:d529dd0c...  RepoTags=["docker.io/library/alpine:3","docker.io/library/alpine:latest"]
  sha256:c6348fa8...  RepoTags=["docker.io/library/busybox:latest"]

So `API_DOCKER_TEST_HOST=unix:///run/user/1000/podman/podman.sock prove -lr
t/` fails on that one file, and has been failing on it for as long as those
dangling images have been there. The same run against Docker
(unix:///var/run/docker.sock, 29.7.2, API 1.55) is green, because that store
has no untagged image.

The fix is the emptiness test the code meant to make:

  my $tags = $images->[0]->RepoTags;
  my $name = ref $tags eq 'ARRAY' && @$tags ? $tags->[0] : $images->[0]->Id;

Better still, pick the first image in the list that HAS a tag, and fall back
to an Id only when none does -- inspect by Id works on both engines, so
either is correct, but the current expression is right for neither.

While measuring this, `alpine:latest` was pulled into both stores:
t/containers_stats_error.t's live subtest needs it and answered
`404 no such image: docker.io/library/alpine:latest: image not known`
without it, on both engines. That may deserve a skip rather than a failure.
